    "markdown": "## SearchApi is a real‑time SERP (Search Engine Results Page) scraping service that provides structured JSON data from Google and other search engines, offering features like proxy management, CAPTCHA solving, geo‑targeting, and high‑accuracy scraping.\n\n## What SearchApi Does\n\nSearchApi (searchapi.io) is designed to extract search engine data reliably and at scale. Key capabilities include:\n\n- Real‑time Google SERP scraping with JSON output. [0](https://www.searchapi.io/)\n- Automatic proxy rotation and CAPTCHA solving, mimicking real user behavior. [1](https://github.com/SearchApi)\n- Precise geo‑targeting down to coordinate level. [0](https://www.searchapi.io/)\n- High success rate (99.9%) for search requests. [0](https://www.searchapi.io/)\n- Support for multiple engines (Google, Bing, YouTube, Maps, etc.) via community integrations. [1](https://github.com/SearchApi)\n\n## Example Usage\n\nA typical Google SERP request looks like:\n\n```\ncurl --get https://www.searchapi.io/api/v1/search \\\n  -d engine=\"google\" \\\n  -d q=\"chatgpt\"\n```\n\nThis returns structured JSON including metadata, organic results, knowledge graph, and more. [0](https://www.searchapi.io/)\n\n## Related Ecosystem\n\nSearchApi maintains open‑source tools and integrations such as:\n\n- wreq-ruby (HTTP client with browser fingerprinting)\n- n8n-nodes-searchapi (workflow automation node)\n- Google Maps, Flights, Ads research tools built on top of SearchApi’s data pipelines [1](https://github.com/SearchApi)\n\n## SearchApi vs. Simil",
